upported\"` | [x] |\n| 14 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:674) | `!(data && datalen >= 6)`: no IDAT chunk at all (`datalen==0`, `malloc(0)!=NULL`) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"corrupt zlib structure in DEFLATE stream\"` | [x] |\n| 15 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:674) | `!(data && datalen >= 6)`: IDAT present but total payload `< 6` bytes (1…5) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"corrupt zlib structure in DEFLATE stream\"` | [x] |\n| 16 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:682) | `(data[0] & 0x0f) != 0x08` — zlib CM ≠ 8 (e.g. CMF `0x78`→ok, `0x79`,`0x00`,`0x0f`→fail) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"only zlib compression method (RFC 1950) is supported\"` | [x] |\n| 17 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:690) | `(data[0] & 0xf0) > 0x70` — zlib CINFO `> 7` (CMF `0x88`,`0x98`,…,`0xf8`) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"innapropriate window size detected\"` | [x] |\n| 18 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:698) | `data[1] & 0x20` — zlib FDICT set (FLG e.g. `0x20`,`0x3f`,`0xff`) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"preset dictionary is present and not supported\"` | [x] |\n| 19 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:706) | `cp_out_size(&img,4) < 1`, i.e. `(img.w+1)*img.h*4 < 1` | reason `\"invalid image size found\"` — **unreachable**: rows 7/8/9 already force `w>=1`, `h>=1`, `w*h*4 < INT_MAX`, so the product is in `[4, INT_MAX)`. Proven unreachable; the test asserts C and Rust agree over the whole reachable `w`/`h` boundary set instead | [x] |\n| 20 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:714) | `cp_out_size(&img,bpp) < 1` | reason `\"invalid image size found\"` — **unreachable** for the same reason (`bpp ∈ {1,2,3,4}`) | [x] |\n| 21 | `load_png_mem` (lib.c:723) | `cp_inflate(...)` returns 0 (any of rows 27-32) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"DEFLATE algorithm failed\"` — note `cp_error_reason` is **overwritten**, the inner reason is lost | [x] |\n| 22 | `load_png_mem`→`cp_unfilter` (lib.c:424, 731) | row-0 filter byte `> 4` (5…255) | `pix=NULL`, reason `\"invalid filter byte found\"` | [x] |\n| 23 | `load_png_mem`→`cp_unfilter` (lib.c:458, 731) | filter byte of any row `y >= 1` is `> 4` | `pix=NULL`, reaso