n_base`, `cp_dist_extra_bits`, `cp_dist_base` | read all bytes of all six tables from both `.so`s via `dlsym` and compare | [x] |","-| 70 | `cp_error_reason` | `NULL` before the first call; set to the identical string after each failing call; **left untouched** by a successful call | [x] |","+| # | entry point(s) | configuration | test | [x] |","+|---|----------------|---------------|------|-----|","+| 69 | `cp_fixed_table`, `cp_permutation_order`, `cp_len_extra_bits`, `cp_len_base`, `cp_dist_extra_bits`, `cp_dist_base` | read **all** bytes of all six tables from both `.so`s via `dlsym` and compare (320 / 19 / 31 / 124 / 32 / 128 bytes). `nm -S` also shows identical symbol *sizes* | `data_table_contents`, `symbol_parity` | [x] |","+| 70 | `cp_error_reason` | `NULL` before the first call; set to the identical string after a failing call; **left untouched** by a successful call (asserted) | `error_reason_lifecycle` | [x] |","+","+## Additional C quirks confirmed by the differential tests","+","+1. `cp_stored`'s `bits_left / 8 <= LEN` check is written backwards, so **every**","+   multi-stored-block stream is rejected — including anything flate2 produces at","+   level 0 for input larger than 64 KiB (`ERRORS.md` row 26).","+2. Chunk CRCs and the zlib adler32 are never checked.","+3. A declared IHDR width of 0 yields `w == 1` and therefore `img.w == 0`: a","+   zero-pixel-wide image that the C code happily accepts.","+4. On the error path `img.w` / `img.h` retain the values reached before the","+   failure; only `pix` is reset to `NULL`.","+5. `cp_convert` / `cp_depalette` write `w*h` pixels, so exactly `img.w*img.h*4`","+   bytes of the returned buffer are defined; the tail of the `(img.w+1)*img.h*4`","+   allocation holds leftover unfiltered bytes (and, for `w < 3` with `bpp == 1`,","+   never-written `malloc` memory). The tests compare exactly `img.w*img.h*4`.","+6. Only bit depth 8 is supported, and interlacing (even the legal Adam7 value 1)","+   is rejected."]}],"originalFile":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A / Phase B)\n\n## Build-time configuration\n\n* `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` has **no** `option()`, no `target_compile_definitions`,\n  no `#ifdef`/`#if` anywhere in `src/lib.c` or `include/lib.h` (verified with\n  `grep -n '#if\\|#ifdef\\|#ifndef\\|option(\\|_DEFINITIONS' c_src -r`). The only\n  build-time knob that matters is `NDEBUG`, and it is **not** defined, so\n  `assert()` is live (see `ERRORS.md` §C).\n* Consequently `Cargo.toml` declares `[features] default = []` and the single\n  valid feature combination is the empty one:\n\n  | # | feature combination | `cargo check` | `cargo test` |\n  |---|---------------------|---------------|--------------|\n  | F1 | `--no-default-features` (empty)   | ok | ok |\n  | F2 | `--no-default-features --features default` (== F1) | ok | ok |\n  | F3 | `--all-features` (== F1)          | ok | ok |\n\n  Both cargo profiles are also verified: `dev` (overflow checks on,\n  `panic=unwind`) and `release` (`panic=abort`, optimised).\n\n## Run-time configuration axes actually branched on by the C code\n\n| axis | source | values |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| colour type → `bpp` | `lib.c:555-580` | `0→1`, `2→3`, `3→1`, `4→2`, `6→4` |\n| indexed vs direct | `lib.c:738` | `cp_depalette` (colour type 3) vs `cp_convert` |\n| `cp_convert` pixel builder | `lib.c:468-481` | `switch (bpp)` = 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n| alpha of indexed pixel | `lib.c:485-493` | `trns == NULL` / `index >= trns_len` / else |\n| row-0 filter | `lib.c:407-426` | 0, 1, 2 (no-op!), 3, 4 (`paeth(a,0,0)`) |\n| row-`y>0` filter | `lib.c:431-460` | 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 |\n| back-reference copy | `lib.c:284-291` | `distance == 1` → `memset`, else byte loop |\n| DEFLATE block type | `lib.c:324-354` | 0 stored, 1 fixed, 2 dynamic |\n| block chaining | `lib.c:321-356` | single (BFINAL=1) vs several blocks |\n| bit-buffer refill | `lib.c:84-95` | from `words[]` vs from `final_word` |\n| input alignment | `lib.c:305-315` | `first_bytes` 0..3 |\n| input tail | `lib.c:308-314` | `last_bytes` 0..3 (`final_word_available` 0/1) |\n| chunk scan | `lib.c:377-401` | `cp_chunk` (must be *next*) vs `cp_find` (search) |\n| chunk order | `lib.c:647-672` | the `first`/`png.p` rewind dance for PLTE/tRNS/IDAT |\n| zlib header | `lib.c:682-704` | `CM`, `CINFO` 0..7, `FLEVEL`, `FDICT=0` |\n\n## The table\n\nLegend for “configuration”: `ct` = colour type, `f` = per-row filter bytes,\n`bt` = DEFLATE block type. Every row is driven by **many randomised inputs**\n(deterministic `splitmix64` seed, see `tests/common/mod.rs::Rng`), not a single\nhand-picked value.\n\n### `cp_inflate` — the lowest-level public entry point\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 fixed, literals only, in-ptr **align 0** (`first_bytes=0`), `in_bytes%4==0`, `out_bytes` exact | [x] |\n| 2 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 fixed, literals only, in-ptr **align 3** (`first_bytes=1`) | [x] |\n| 3 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 fixed, literals only, in-ptr **align 2** (`first_bytes=2`) | [x] |\n| 4 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 fixed, literals only, in-ptr **align 1** (`first_bytes=3`) | [x] |\n| 5 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1, `in_bytes-first_bytes ≡ 0 (mod 4)` → `last_bytes=0`, `final_word_available=0` | [x] |\n| 6 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1, `≡ 1 (mod 4)` → `last_bytes=1`, `final_word_available=1` | [x] |\n| 7 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1, `≡ 2 (mod 4)` → `last_bytes=2` | [x] |\n| 8 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1, `≡ 3 (mod 4)` → `last_bytes=3` | [x] |\n| 9 | `cp_inflate` | full cross product align(4) × tail(4) = 16 combinations, random payloads | [x] |\n| 10 | `cp_inflate` | bt=0 stored, single block, `LEN` 1..4096, all 4 input alignments | [x] |\n| 11 | `cp_inflate` | bt=0 stored, `LEN == 0` (empty block, `memcpy(...,0)`) | [x] |\n| 12 | `cp_inflate` | bt=2 dynamic (flate2 level 1) | [x] |\n| 13 | `cp_inflate` | bt=2 dynamic (flate2 level 6, default) | [x] |\n| 14 | `cp_inflate` | bt=2 dynamic (flate2 level 9) | [x] |\n| 15 | `cp_inflate` | bt=2 dynamic on highly repetitive data → long matches, code-length RLE symbols 16/17/18 in the header | [x] |\n| 16 | `cp_inflate` | several blocks: fixed + fixed, BFINAL only on the last | [x] |\n| 17 | `cp_inflate` | several blocks: fixed + dynamic + fixed | [x] |\n| 18 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 with back-reference **distance == 1** → `memset` branch, lengths 3..258 | [x] |\n| 19 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 with back-reference **distance > 1**, non-overlapping | [x] |\n| 20 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 with **overlapping** back-reference (`length > distance`, distance 2..8) | [x] |\n| 21 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 sweeping **every length code** 257..285 (all `cp_len_base`/`cp_len_extra_bits` entries incl. 258/sym 285) | [x] |\n| 22 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 sweeping **every distance code** 0..29 (all `cp_dist_base`/`cp_dist_extra_bits` entries, up to 32768) | [x] |\n| 23 | `cp_inflate` | bt=1 literal alphabet boundaries: values 0..143 (8-bit codes), 144..255 (9-bit codes), symbol 256 (7-bit) | [x] |\n| 24 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes` **larger** than the stream produces (slack tail must stay untouched — buffers pre-filled with `0xCD`) | [x] |\n| 25 | `cp_inflate` | output > 64 KiB (multiple flate2 blocks, distances up to 32768) | [x] |\n| 26 | `cp_inflate` | 1-byte output, 1-byte input tail combinations | [x] |\n\n### `load_png_mem` — colour type / `bpp` surface\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 27 | `load_png_mem` | ct=0 grey, bpp=1 → `cp_convert` case 1, random sizes | [x] |\n| 28 | `load_png_mem` | ct=2 RGB, bpp=3 → `cp_convert` case 3 | [x] |\n| 29 | `load_png_mem` | ct=4 grey+alpha, bpp=2 → `cp_convert` case 2 | [x] |\n| 30 | `load_png_mem` | ct=6 RGBA, bpp=4 → `cp_convert` case 4 | [x] |\n| 31 | `load_png_mem` | ct=3 indexed, PLTE 256 entries, **no** tRNS → alpha=255 branch | [x] |\n| 32 | `load_png_mem` | ct=3 indexed, PLTE + tRNS with `trns_len == 256` → `trns[index]` branch | [x] |\n| 33 | `load_png_mem` | ct=3 indexed, PLTE + tRNS with `trns_len < 256` → mixed `trns[index]` / 255 branches | [x] |\n| 34 | `load_png_mem` | ct=3 indexed, PLTE + **zero-length** tRNS (`trns_len == 0`) → always 255 | [x] |\n| 35 | `load_png_mem` | ct=3 indexed, PLTE with **fewer than 256 entries** while indices exceed it (`plte[c*3]` reads past the chunk — identical OOB read of the identical buffer) | [x] |\n| 36 | `load_png_mem` | ct=3 indexed, tRNS **longer** than 256 | [x] |\n| 37 | `load_png_mem` | ct≠3 but PLTE and/or tRNS present → both ignored by `cp_convert`, but they still move `first` | [x] |\n\n### `load_png_mem` — filter surface (`cp_unfilter`)\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 38 | `load_png_mem` | every row filter = 0 (None), all 5 colour types | [x] |\n| 39 | `load_png_mem` | every row filter = 1 (Sub); row 0 uses the `x=bpp` start, rows>0 the `x=0` start | [x] |\n| 40 | `load_png_mem` | every row filter = 2 (Up); **row 0 case 2 is a no-op in C** | [x] |\n| 41 | `load_png_mem` | every row filter = 3 (Average); row 0 uses `raw[x-bpp]/2`, rows>0 `(raw[x-bpp]+prev[x])/2` | [x] |\n| 42 | `load_png_mem` | every row filter = 4 (Paeth); row 0 uses `cp_paeth(a,0,0)`, rows>0 the full Paeth | [x] |\n| 43 | `load_png_mem` | random filter per row (0..4), h up to 32, all colour types | [x] |\n| 44 | `load_png_mem` | h == 1 → the `for y=1; y<h` loop never runs | [x] |\n| 45 | `load_png_mem` | `w*bpp <= bpp` (w == 1) → the `for x=bpp; x<len` loops never run | [x] |\n\n### `load_png_mem` — image-shape surface\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 46 | `load_png_mem` | 1×1 (smallest legal image), all 5 colour types | [x] |\n| 47 | `load_png_mem` | 1×N (N up to 64), all colour types | [x] |\n| 48 | `load_png_mem` | N×1, all colour types | [x] |\n| 49 | `load_png_mem` | w == 2 with bpp == 1 → `out` region overlaps the converted pixels differently ((w+1)·h·3 > w·h·4) | [x] |\n| 50 | `load_png_mem` | w == 3 with bpp == 1 → exact boundary `(w+1)·h·3 == w·h·4` | [x] |\n| 51 | `load_png_mem` | larger images: 64×64, 127×33, 256×3 (random sizes ≤ 300×300) | [x] |\n| 52 | `load_png_mem` | randomised `w`×`h` × colour type cross product (many seeds) | [x] |\n\n### `load_png_mem` — container / chunk surface\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 53 | `load_png_mem` | one IDAT chunk holding the whole zlib stream | [x] |\n| 54 | `load_png_mem` | zlib stream split over 2..17 **contiguous** IDAT chunks (random split points) | [x] |\n| 55 | `load_png_mem` | zero-length IDAT chunks interleaved with non-empty ones | [x] |\n| 56 | `load_png_mem` | **non-contiguous** IDATs (unknown chunk in between) → only the leading run is collected (`cp_chunk` requires the *next* chunk) | [x] |\n| 57 | `load_png_mem` | unknown ancillary chunks (`gAMA`, `sRGB`, `tEXt`, `bKGD`) before the IDATs | [x] |\n| 58 | `load_png_mem` | unknown chunks *between* IHDR and PLTE, and after tRNS | [x] |\n| 59 | `load_png_mem` | tRNS **before** PLTE in the file → `cp_find(tRNS)` starts after PLTE ⇒ `trns == NULL` | [x] |\n| 60 | `load_png_mem` | tRNS **after** the IDATs → `first` jumps past them ⇒ `datalen == 0` ⇒ rejection | [x] |\n| 61 | `load_png_mem` | IEND present / absent; trailing garbage after IEND; `png_length` > real PNG length | [x] |\n| 62 | `load_png_mem` | zlib `CMF` with `CINFO` 0..7 (`0x08,0x18,0x28,…,0x78`), all accepted | [x] |\n| 63 | `load_png_mem` | zlib `FLG` with all `FLEVEL` values and a deliberately wrong `FCHECK` (never validated), `FDICT=0` | [x] |\n| 64 | `load_png_mem` | IDAT payload contains a **stored** DEFLATE block (bt=0) | [x] |\n| 65 | `load_png_mem` | IDAT payload contains a **fixed** DEFLATE block (bt=1) | [x] |\n| 66 | `load_png_mem` | IDAT payload from flate2 levels 0..9 (dynamic + stored mixes) | [x] |\n| 67 | `load_png_mem` | wrong (garbage) chunk CRCs and wrong adler32 — never validated by the C code | [x] |\n| 68 | `load_png_mem` | IHDR length > 13 (extra trailing bytes in the chunk, still `>= minlen`) | [x] |\n\n### exported data symbols\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 69 | `cp_fixed_table`, `cp_permutation_order`, `cp_len_extra_bits`, `cp_len_base`, `cp_dist_extra_bits`, `cp_dist_base` | read all bytes of all six tables from both `.so`s via `dlsym` and compare | [x] |\n| 70 | `cp_error_reason` | `NULL` before the first call; set to the identical string after each failing call; **left untouched** by a successful call | [x] |\n","userModified":false}}
