{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_aiaowsmzfoxxafpl7hig6qnlwjyinmm5guy52i5bskgebgikoifq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01MMpyjGjXBmj4Ht9PszgjuV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/chunks.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''            let r = diff_png_abort(\n                &png,\n                png.len() as i32,\n                &format!(\"idat len={len:#010X} n={nidat}\"),\n            );\n            eprintln!(\"row74 len={len:#010X} n={nidat} -> {:?}\", match &r.outcome {\n                Outcome::Signaled(s) => format!(\"signal {s}\"),\n                Outcome::Exited(c, d) => format!(\"exit {c}, {} bytes\", d.len()),\n            });''','''            // Measured outcome classes for this row (C and Rust agree on all of\n            // them):\n            //   len = 0x0000000C, n = 1          -> SIGABRT (a live assert())\n            //   len >= 0x7FFFFFF4, n >= 2        -> SIGSEGV (cp_chunk's `int`\n            //                                       offset goes negative, so the\n            //                                       cursor walks ~2 GiB backwards)\n            //   len = 0xFFFFFFF4                 -> SIGALRM: `len + 12` wraps to\n            //                                       0, so cp_chunk returns the\n            //                                       same chunk forever and the\n            //                                       IDAT loop *never terminates*\n            //   everything else                  -> a normal rejection\n            diff_png_abort(\n                &png,\n                png.len() as i32,\n                &format!(\"idat len={len:#010X} n={nidat}\"),\n            );''')\ns=s.replace('''        let r = diff_png_abort(\n            &png,\n            png.len() as i32,\n            &format!(\"datalen overflow n={n} len={len:#010X}\"),\n        );\n        eprintln!(\"row75 n={n} len={len:#010X}