{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dcdqmggxat23e3yjftoeiplw4z2xyhfkx2rwnzntsdc2colyhs3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's what I found and fixed.\n\n## Result\n\n`./verify.sh` → **ALL VERIFICATION PASSED** — 98 differential tests, both cargo profiles, symbol parity 9/9.\n\n## Phases\n\n**Phase A** — `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (52 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (76 rows). All 128 rows checked off, no gaps. `Cargo.toml` had no `[features]` and `c_src` has zero `#ifdef`/`option()`, so there is exactly one real feature combination (verified mechanically, not assumed).\n\n**Phase B** (76 rows) — drove `cp_inflate` directly (all 4 input alignments × all 4 tail residues, every length code 257–285, every distance code 0–29, every literal, every block type and chain) plus `load_png_mem` across all colour types, filters, shapes and chunk layouts. Successful decodes are also checked against an **independent RFC 2083 reference decoder**, so \"both wrong the same way\" can't pass.\n\n**Phase C** (52 rows) — every rejection branch, plus all 10 live `assert()`s.\n\n## Real fixes to the Rust\n\n1. **`assert()` is live in the C build** — `CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the `.so` imports `__assert_fail`. The translation had dropped all 10 asserts as \"debugging aids\". I added all 10 as `abort()` calls. Two were only reachable by poking the exported writable tables; one (`cp_ptr`'s `!(bits_left & 7)`) I derived analytically (`bits_left ≡ -c0 mod 8` after a `final_word` refill) and built an 11-byte stream for it. This also means the Rust no longer *infinite-loops* where C aborts.\n\n2. **`cp_dynamic` smashes its own stack** — `uint8_t lens[288+32]` is written up to index 456. Confirmed with `-fstack-protector-all`. The old Rust used an oversized array, so C hung (`lens[376]` aliases the loop variable `n`, rewinding it forever) while Rust returned. I reproduced gcc's `-O0` frame layout byte for byte from `objdump`, including `lens[-1]` being the top byte of the `s` pointer and `lens[n++]` storing `n` *before* the byte.\n\n## C quirks confirmed, not \"fixed\"\n\n`cp_ptr` copies the wrong bytes for small stored blocks at certain alignments; `bits_left/8 <= LEN` is backwards so every multi-stored-block stream is rejected; `datalen == 6` aborts; tRNS before PLTE is silently ignored; `cp_chunk` uses a **signed** `int offset = len + 12` while `cp_find` uses unsigned — a declared length of `0xFFFFFFF4` makes the IDAT loop never terminate. All reproduced identically (`tests/chunks.rs` sees matching SIGABRT, SIGSEGV *and* infinite loops).\n\n## Two harness traps worth noting\n\nTwo apparent divergences were my test's fault, not the translation's: the C reads past short PLTE chunks (fixed by a padded buffer), and `load_png_mem` lets `cp_inflate` write past `img.pix` when `bpp < 4`, corrupting heap metadata — so both children must be `fork()`ed back-to-back from identical parent state (`run_forked_pair`). Without that, the test measures the parent's allocator history.\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified (original mtimes intact; only `c_src/build/` was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1313,"cache_read_input_tokens":457306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1313,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"89f53f94-7b24-49ff-9a7f-5be92497be56","uuid":"18e7a4ed-5c0a-411c-baa0-48d7933af719","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:33:17.476Z"}
